---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const video = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'VideoObject',
  name: 'ArtemisKit Introduction: Get Started',
  description: 'Learn how to install the ArtemisKit CLI, configure a provider, write a scenario and inspect a first evaluation result.',
  thumbnailUrl: 'https://www.artemiskit.dev/videos/artemiskit-introduction-thumbnail.png',
  contentUrl: 'https://www.artemiskit.dev/videos/artemiskit-introduction.mp4',
  uploadDate: '2026-10-27', duration: 'PT1M20.8S'
};
---
<Layout title="ArtemisKit introduction and getting started video" description="Watch an introduction to ArtemisKit, from installing the CLI and configuring a provider to running a first scenario and understanding its result." image="/videos/artemiskit-introduction-thumbnail.png">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(video)} />
  <section class="ak-page-head"><div class="ak-wrap">
    <div class="ak-kicker">ArtemisKit introduction</div>
    <h1>Get started with ArtemisKit</h1>
    <p>See how a small, repeatable check helps you inspect what your AI was asked to do and what happened.</p>
    <video controls preload="none" poster="/videos/artemiskit-introduction-poster.webp" width="100%" aria-label="ArtemisKit introduction and getting started video">
      <source src="/videos/artemiskit-introduction.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      <track kind="captions" src="/videos/artemiskit-introduction.en.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default />
      Your browser does not support embedded video. <a href="/videos/artemiskit-introduction.mp4">Download the introduction video</a>.
    </video>
  </div></section>
  <div class="ak-wrap"><article class="ak-prose">
    <h2>Video transcript</h2>
    <p>Your AI answer looks right. But does it still work when the request changes, or when an important detail is missing? If you can't repeat the check, every prompt edit becomes guesswork.</p>
    <p>ArtemisKit is an open-source toolkit for evaluating AI behavior against the cases and expectations you choose. It gives you a repeatable way to see what was tested, what happened, and where you still need to investigate.</p>
    <p>Let's run a first test. The command-line tool needs Bun. With Bun installed, install the CLI, and check its version. Next, configure a supported model provider using your own credentials.</p>
    <p>Create a small YAML scenario. Give a case a prompt, then specify what the response must contain. For this example, the expected value is four. Run the scenario with ArtemisKit using the command on screen. Here, we've connected a local model through an OpenAI-compatible endpoint. ArtemisKit records the response and the check alongside the run details.</p>
    <p>This single case passed. That tells us only that this model, in this run, met this one check. Now add a boundary case, change one thing, and run it again. Discover more at artemiskit.dev. Your AI has a job. Test it for that job.</p>
    <p>Ready to try it? Follow the <a href="/docs/getting-started/">getting started guide</a> for the prerequisites, commands and next steps.</p>
  </article></div>
</Layout>
